**RECITALS**

WHEREAS, Producer has recently ceased agricultural operations on their property located at 1234 Harvest Lane, Springfield, IL (the “Farm”), citing financial difficulties and adverse weather conditions, leading to a total crop failure and the discontinuation of livestock rearing;

WHEREAS, Buyer has shifted its purchasing strategy to focus on sourcing agricultural commodities exclusively from out-of-state suppliers, emphasizing greater supply chain efficiency and more favorable pricing structures, which has resulted in a reduced demand for local products;

WHEREAS, Producer and Buyer have mutually decided to dissolve any existing agreements regarding the supply of agricultural products due to the Producer's inability to meet quality standards and delivery timelines.

**NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the challenges faced by both parties, the following points are outlined:**

**1. DEFINITIONS**  
For the purposes of this Discussion, the following terms shall have the meanings set forth below:

1.1 “Crops” refers solely to the agricultural produce

